     "claim": "D_hook",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "Over about three weeks in October 2002 (2-22 October) two snipers shot people at random in the Washington, DC area; the FBI calls it '23 days of random attacks'. The attacks ended with the arrests at the rest stop on 24 October 2002.",
     "urls": [
      "https://www.fbi.gov/news/stories/2007/october/snipers_102407",
      "https://britannica.com/print/article/1987489",
      "https://bac-lac.wayback.archive-it.org/web/20071123221247/http://www.cbc.ca/news/background/sniper",
      "https://wtop.com/local/2026/05/without-warning-exhibit-tells-story-of-victims-takedown-in-2002-dc-sniper-case/"
     ]
    },
    {
     "claim": "D_rest",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "At about 1 a.m. on 24 October 2002 a truck driver (Ron Lantz; not named on screen) saw the Caprice at a rest stop off Interstate 70 near Myersville, Maryland, and called 911; trucks were pulled across the exit; police found two men asleep in the car and arrested Muhammad and Malvo without incident (custody at about 3:19-3:30 a.m.). An early CNN transcript credited 'a motorist' and a rest-stop attendant; narration says 'a trucker'.",
     "urls": [
      "https://us.cnn.com/TRANSCRIPTS/0210/24/bn.04.html",
      "https://wtop.com/local/2026/05/without-warning-exhibit-tells-story-of-victims-takedown-in-2002-dc-sniper-case/",
      "https://northernvirginiamag.com/culture/culture-features/2019/11/07/a-collective-timeline-of-the-dc-sniper-case-from-2002-to-2019/",
      "https://cbsnews.com/news/trucker-im-no-hero",
      "https://www.foxnews.com/story/sniper-spotting-trucker-a-humble-hero",
      "https://www.trucknews.com/transportation/trucker-instrumental-in-stopping-d-c-sniper/1000005972",
      "https://www.officer.com/command-hq/supplies-services/public-awareness/news/10819850/officers-recall-end-to-dc-snipers-terror-grip",
      "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/amp/wbna3339881"
     ]
    }
